WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.166 --> 00:00:05.300
Intense action is a hallmark of the Kalos League.

2
00:00:05.766 --> 00:00:07.666
After many hard-fought battles,

3
00:00:07.733 --> 00:00:10.733
Ash has managed to make it to the semifinal round,

4
00:00:10.866 --> 00:00:15.066
and Goodra has rejoined his team for the full battle ahead.

5
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.433
Now, with a six-Pokémon lineup,

6
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:21.900
Ash is about to fulfill a promise and face off against his rival, Sawyer.

7
00:00:27.233 --> 00:00:28.733
Rhypo, no!

8
00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:31.800
Rhyperior.

9
00:00:32.299 --> 00:00:35.633
Rhyperior is unable to battle! Charizard is the winner!

10
00:00:36.766 --> 00:00:38.933
And Remo's Rhyperior is defeated,

11
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.000
leaving him with one Pokémon left.

12
00:00:41.066 --> 00:00:43.466
Ladies and gentlemen, it's crunch time.

13
00:00:44.266 --> 00:00:46.500
- Wow!
- Pika, pika!

14
00:00:46.566 --> 00:00:47.700
So strong!

15
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.266
In all of Alain's battles up until now, he's only used Metagross and Charizard.

16
00:00:54.866 --> 00:00:57.633
His strength is still as incalculable as ever.

17
00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:58.533
Right.

18
00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:05.666
Now, if I win this battle, next stop, the final round.

19
00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:06.700
Got it?

20
00:01:10.633 --> 00:01:12.600
This Pokémon will beat them all!

21
00:01:12.766 --> 00:01:14.466
Go, Garchoo!

22
00:01:20.466 --> 00:01:24.966
Since losing last time, we've trained and pushed ourselves to the limit!

23
00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:29.233
Day after day, all we could think about was defeating you.

24
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:35.300
You're about to see the results of that training! Prepare for a shock!

25
00:01:36.933 --> 00:01:39.266
Now, Garchoo, go!

26
00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.833
Mega Evolve!

27
00:01:47.166 --> 00:01:50.433
What a sight! Garchomp has Mega Evolved!

28
00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.433
Remo means business!

29
00:01:53.233 --> 00:01:55.400
Now, watch and learn!

30
00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.933
Garchoo, Draco Meteor!

31
00:02:05.833 --> 00:02:06.666
Dodge it!

32
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.600
You must admit, that's one powerful move!

33
00:02:15.833 --> 00:02:17.366
Respond to my heart!

34
00:02:17.666 --> 00:02:20.333
Now, Key Stone, Beyond Evolution!

35
00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.633
Mega Evolve!

36
00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.833
Out of this world! Alain's Charizard has Mega Evolved, too!

37
00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.966
It's a clash of dueling Mega-Evolved Pokémon!

38
00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.500
That's what I like to see! Now, Garchoo, Dragon Rush!

39
00:02:51.866 --> 00:02:53.433
Dragon Claw!

40
00:02:56.733 --> 00:02:58.166
Charizard, throw it!

41
00:03:00.866 --> 00:03:02.533
- Oh, no!
- Use Flamethrower!

42
00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.533
- Dragon Claw!
- Dragon Claw!

43
00:03:13.266 --> 00:03:14.266
Garchoo!

44
00:03:16.366 --> 00:03:18.200
Garchomp is unable to battle!

45
00:03:18.266 --> 00:03:20.533
Charizard wins! The winner is Alain!

46
00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:25.466
He did it! It's Alain who will advance to the final round!

47
00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:36.966
Pika.

48
00:03:38.766 --> 00:03:41.000
That was great battling, Charizard.

49
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.233
♪ I stand tall 'cause I know I'm a winner ♪

50
00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:03.133
♪ Knock me down I'll just get up again ♪

51
00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:07.133
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

52
00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.366
♪ Pokémon ♪

53
00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:10.333
♪ Pokémon ♪

54
00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.566
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

55
00:04:11.633 --> 00:04:14.733
♪ I stand tall 'cause I know I'm a winner ♪

56
00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:15.933
♪ Pokémon ♪

57
00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:17.933
♪ Pokémon ♪

58
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.366
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

59
00:04:30.433 --> 00:04:32.833
All right, it's time to battle Sawyer.

60
00:04:35.366 --> 00:04:37.266
I know I've made mistakes.

61
00:04:37.333 --> 00:04:40.033
You're still with me, and that means a lot.

62
00:04:40.433 --> 00:04:42.166
You're the best team ever.

63
00:04:43.533 --> 00:04:45.800
I believe in you more than I can say.

64
00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.033
Let's win this thing together!

65
00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.866
It's finally time.

66
00:05:08.433 --> 00:05:09.966
Ash is battling Sawyer.

67
00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:11.966
I'm getting kind of nervous.

68
00:05:12.533 --> 00:05:16.133
Clemont, didn't you tell me Ash lost to Sawyer a while back?

69
00:05:16.433 --> 00:05:18.833
I did. Never count Sawyer out.

70
00:05:19.166 --> 00:05:20.566
Wait till you see this.

71
00:05:20.633 --> 00:05:24.566
Their battling styles are different. Still, he reminds me of Ash.

72
00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:28.566
It's like the same sort of battle vibe is inside both of them.

73
00:05:28.633 --> 00:05:30.600
Wow. You think so?

74
00:05:31.066 --> 00:05:34.533
Sawyer's been analyzing Ash's style to catch up to him.

75
00:05:34.733 --> 00:05:38.100
I'd say that's exactly what you're referring to, Tierno.

76
00:05:38.166 --> 00:05:41.833
A match between a trainer like Ash, who battles with passion,

77
00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.133
and Sawyer, who operates using cool and calm analysis.

78
00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:50.600
They're opposites. I'm looking forward to seeing what kind of battle this will be.

79
00:05:51.066 --> 00:05:51.900
Yeah.

80
00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:56.133
Now, the second battle of the semifinal round.

81
00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.633
Our trainers are making their entrances.

82
00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:08.200
All right, Ash! Win it!

83
00:06:08.666 --> 00:06:09.933
You can do it!

84
00:06:12.533 --> 00:06:14.033
Che! Pin-che!

85
00:06:20.666 --> 00:06:22.633
Get a shot of their faces first.

86
00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.633
Posthaste!

87
00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:28.866
I'm too tired to take head shots of a completely clueless twerp.

88
00:06:29.466 --> 00:06:32.133
We should be filming my radiant beauty.

89
00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.500
Chin up. Just a little more stuff.

90
00:06:34.566 --> 00:06:36.966
This is the last battle of the livelong day.

91
00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:41.766
It's time.

92
00:06:42.366 --> 00:06:43.933
I'll be waiting for you.

93
00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:45.433
Yeah.

94
00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.866
It's all gonna work out.

95
00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:52.033
The person I admire so much will win in the end.

96
00:06:53.666 --> 00:06:55.066
And I'll be waiting.

97
00:06:55.566 --> 00:06:56.766
I wanna beat Ash.

98
00:06:57.733 --> 00:06:59.333
I've just gotta beat him.

99
00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:00.833
And I will.

100
00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:02.133
All right.

101
00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:03.966
Bring it on.

102
00:07:04.466 --> 00:07:06.566
- This one's mine.
- Hmm.

103
00:07:09.166 --> 00:07:12.266
And now for the battlefield.

104
00:07:12.966 --> 00:07:15.666
It's a forest!

105
00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:20.433
Ash versus Sawyer.

106
00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:23.733
Competing head-to-head in our next semifinal battle.

107
00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:26.466
Each trainer will have the use of six Pokémon

108
00:07:26.533 --> 00:07:28.366
and substitutions are allowed.

109
00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:32.666
When all six of either trainer's Pokémon are unable to continue,

110
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.733
the battle will be over.

111
00:07:35.166 --> 00:07:40.200
When three Pokémon on one side are unable to continue, the battlefield will change.

112
00:07:41.966 --> 00:07:44.166
Trainers, begin!

113
00:07:44.533 --> 00:07:46.600
Hawlucha, I choose you!

114
00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.466
Hawlucha!

115
00:08:02.133 --> 00:08:02.966
Lucha.

116
00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:04.866
Hawlucha?

117
00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.233
It looks different.

118
00:08:07.433 --> 00:08:08.666
Wow, you're right.

119
00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.600
See, yesterday...

120
00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:16.766
Hmm? What's wrong, Hawlucha?

121
00:08:17.033 --> 00:08:18.233
Cha.

122
00:08:18.966 --> 00:08:20.100
Huh?

123
00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:22.333
Hawlucha.

124
00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:25.900
Hawlucha.

125
00:08:26.366 --> 00:08:27.366
That's dramatic.

126
00:08:27.633 --> 00:08:30.766
You need to make an entrance like a Forest Champion.

127
00:08:30.866 --> 00:08:32.900
- That's important.
- Yeah.

128
00:08:33.466 --> 00:08:35.799
All right, Hawlucha. Looking good.

129
00:08:36.066 --> 00:08:36.900
Dedenne!

130
00:08:38.799 --> 00:08:39.766
Lucha!

131
00:08:43.299 --> 00:08:45.700
So, Hawlucha's gonna be your first Pokémon, huh?

132
00:08:46.166 --> 00:08:48.400
Yeah, we go with Hawlucha first.

133
00:08:49.266 --> 00:08:50.300
Lucha.

134
00:08:50.366 --> 00:08:52.733
Then I'm gonna use Slaking!

135
00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.600
Slak.

136
00:08:56.666 --> 00:08:58.033
It's so cute!

137
00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:02.666
Slaking, the lazy Pokémon.

138
00:09:03.166 --> 00:09:05.333
Slaking lies down most of the time.

139
00:09:05.433 --> 00:09:09.666
It gets up and moves only when there is no more grass close by to eat.

140
00:09:09.733 --> 00:09:11.366
I want a hug!

141
00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:12.800
That's a Slaking.

142
00:09:13.066 --> 00:09:18.666
Slaking has quite a disadvantage against Hawlucha. I wonder what Sawyer's planning.

143
00:09:20.666 --> 00:09:23.466
All right, battle begin!

144
00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:29.633
Let's go, Hawlucha. Make the first move.

145
00:09:29.933 --> 00:09:31.866
- Use Karate Chop!
- Cha!

146
00:09:32.466 --> 00:09:33.333
Ha!

147
00:09:35.933 --> 00:09:36.833
Lucha.

148
00:09:38.433 --> 00:09:41.433
- Slaking.
- Haw-cha?

149
00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:43.200
Now use High Jump Kick!

150
00:09:47.466 --> 00:09:48.300
Cha!

151
00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:50.533
Hawlucha.

152
00:09:51.166 --> 00:09:53.933
Really? While Hawlucha aggressively attacks,

153
00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.866
Slaking's doing nothing at all!

154
00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:58.066
Use X-Scissor!

155
00:09:58.400 --> 00:09:59.400
Hawlucha!

156
00:10:05.533 --> 00:10:07.733
Whenever Hawlucha's having a battle,

157
00:10:07.800 --> 00:10:11.000
it gets worked up by trading blows with its opponent.

158
00:10:11.266 --> 00:10:14.433
- But if its opponent doesn't move...
- Things get difficult.

159
00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:15.533
Mm-hm.

160
00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:19.433
Keep attacking. If it's not gonna move, you'll win the match.

161
00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.100
Now, Karate Chop!

162
00:10:21.766 --> 00:10:24.033
Hawlucha!

163
00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:27.533
Cha! Cha! Cha! Cha! Cha!

164
00:10:29.333 --> 00:10:31.533
Hawlucha, use Karate Chop again!

165
00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:32.700
Lucha!

166
00:10:33.633 --> 00:10:37.966
Hawlucha unleashes fierce attacks. Slaking must be feeling that.

167
00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:39.966
Hawlucha?

168
00:10:40.433 --> 00:10:42.066
Slaking is unfazed.

169
00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:46.366
- I think Slaking's just acting tough.
- Tough? What do you mean?

170
00:10:46.833 --> 00:10:48.300
Slaking, use Slack Off!

171
00:10:48.766 --> 00:10:51.300
Slaking.

172
00:10:51.766 --> 00:10:53.166
- Right now?
- Huh?

173
00:10:53.233 --> 00:10:57.900
Slack Off is a move that allows the user to recover its strength by relaxing.

174
00:10:57.966 --> 00:11:01.200
Even so, if Slaking keeps on taking hits like that,

175
00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.966
it will eventually lose.

176
00:11:03.833 --> 00:11:05.966
I wonder what Sawyer's strategy is.

177
00:11:13.366 --> 00:11:15.433
Who's that Pokémon?

178
00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:23.766
- It's Slaking!
- Slaking!

179
00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:36.500
No doubt about it. Sawyer's got something up his sleeve.

180
00:11:36.566 --> 00:11:39.166
I've gotta beat him before he acts on it!

181
00:11:39.633 --> 00:11:40.900
High Jump Kick, go!

182
00:11:42.333 --> 00:11:43.300
Cha!

183
00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.400
Now, use X-Scissor!

184
00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.333
Haw-cha!

185
00:11:52.433 --> 00:11:53.266
Lucha?

186
00:11:53.333 --> 00:11:55.100
All right, Flying Press!

187
00:11:57.833 --> 00:11:59.766
Lucha!

188
00:12:00.733 --> 00:12:02.700
Slaking, Counter. Let's go!

189
00:12:03.166 --> 00:12:05.300
Slaking!

190
00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:07.333
King!

191
00:12:12.966 --> 00:12:14.166
Hawlucha, no!

192
00:12:15.333 --> 00:12:17.400
- Hawlucha!
- Dedenne!

193
00:12:19.033 --> 00:12:21.633
- Hawlucha is unable to battle.
- King.

194
00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:23.233
Slaking's the winner!

195
00:12:23.866 --> 00:12:26.433
It looked like Hawlucha had the upper hand,

196
00:12:26.500 --> 00:12:28.933
but in one shot, it's out of contention.

197
00:12:30.433 --> 00:12:32.300
Great job. You were awesome.

198
00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:36.200
Now take a good rest. So, that's what you were after all along.

199
00:12:36.666 --> 00:12:39.900
I always thought about using Slaking against Hawlucha.

200
00:12:39.966 --> 00:12:44.566
I knew Hawlucha wouldn't have an easy time if its opponent didn't defend.

201
00:12:45.566 --> 00:12:46.800
I'm impressed.

202
00:12:46.966 --> 00:12:50.433
You took Hawlucha's battling style and used it against it.

203
00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:53.233
Who would've thought of such a tactic?

204
00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:57.166
Sawyer thought through his strategies more than we anticipated.

205
00:12:57.633 --> 00:13:00.300
Now, who will be Ash's second Pokémon?

206
00:13:00.366 --> 00:13:02.566
Talonflame, I choose you!

207
00:13:04.566 --> 00:13:06.933
Talonflame!

208
00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:08.866
Okay, let's do this.

209
00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:10.166
Use Steel Wing!

210
00:13:15.533 --> 00:13:17.466
Slaking, use Slack Off.

211
00:13:17.533 --> 00:13:19.366
King.

212
00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:24.300
Look, it healed itself again.

213
00:13:24.366 --> 00:13:27.933
Maybe they're dragging it out to win again with one attack.

214
00:13:28.366 --> 00:13:31.166
Slaking's gotta be feeling Hawlucha's attacks.

215
00:13:31.533 --> 00:13:35.133
Keep it up! Use Flame Charge and don't let Slaking recover!

216
00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:40.433
Even if Slack Off works, it doesn't change the fact that Slaking's taken damage.

217
00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:43.633
Eventually, that will be an opportunity to strike.

218
00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.066
Use Hammer Arm!

219
00:13:46.533 --> 00:13:49.733
King! Slaking!

220
00:13:51.166 --> 00:13:52.100
King!

221
00:13:52.700 --> 00:13:53.900
Slak!

222
00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:57.200
Yes! Use Brave Bird!

223
00:13:57.266 --> 00:14:01.800
- Talonflame!
- King!

224
00:14:03.133 --> 00:14:06.266
- Slaking.
- Slaking is unable to battle.

225
00:14:06.333 --> 00:14:07.866
Talonflame's the winner!

226
00:14:08.133 --> 00:14:11.500
And Talonflame gets the win with a barrage of attacks!

227
00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:13.200
All right!

228
00:14:13.733 --> 00:14:14.600
Pika!

229
00:14:15.366 --> 00:14:17.133
You were amazing, Slaking.

230
00:14:17.233 --> 00:14:20.033
You did exactly what I was hoping you would do.

231
00:14:25.966 --> 00:14:28.866
All right, Clawitzer, you're up next. Now go!

232
00:14:30.533 --> 00:14:32.700
Claw, Clawitzer.

233
00:14:33.166 --> 00:14:37.333
Clawitzer, it's a Water Type, battling Talonflame, who's a Fire Type.

234
00:14:37.633 --> 00:14:39.033
He's going by the book.

235
00:14:39.566 --> 00:14:41.933
Clawitzer, use Aqua Jet!

236
00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:44.266
Dodge it, quick!

237
00:14:45.566 --> 00:14:47.166
It's following Talonflame!

238
00:14:47.666 --> 00:14:48.500
Talon!

239
00:14:49.766 --> 00:14:52.600
I had no idea you could use Aqua Jet like that.

240
00:14:52.666 --> 00:14:56.966
- Sawyer's strategies are out of the box.
- Kind of reminds me of Ash.

241
00:14:57.433 --> 00:14:59.466
I've been inspired by your ideas,

242
00:14:59.533 --> 00:15:02.533
- and trained hard to think differently.
- Awesome.

243
00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:03.966
Talonflame, dive in!

244
00:15:04.033 --> 00:15:06.633
All right. Clawitzer, use Ice Beam!

245
00:15:08.366 --> 00:15:10.533
Use your smoking hot Flame Charge!

246
00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:16.433
Talonflame!

247
00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:21.233
Look at the way that Flame Charge melted the ice.

248
00:15:21.300 --> 00:15:22.933
- Yippee!
- Denne!

249
00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.200
Aqua Jet, let's go!

250
00:15:26.766 --> 00:15:27.633
Flame!

251
00:15:34.033 --> 00:15:36.400
Talon?

252
00:15:36.466 --> 00:15:38.733
- Talonflame, no!
- Pika.

253
00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:41.466
Talonflame is unable to battle!

254
00:15:41.533 --> 00:15:43.266
Clawitzer's the winner!

255
00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.833
And Clawitzer comes out on top in an aerial battle.

256
00:15:49.066 --> 00:15:50.600
Thanks a lot, Talonflame.

257
00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:53.433
Talonflame's best known for its speed.

258
00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:57.466
If I could make it stop just for a moment, I knew we could win.

259
00:15:58.633 --> 00:15:59.566
Hmm.

260
00:16:04.700 --> 00:16:07.933
What do you know? The twerp's looking rather twerpish.

261
00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:10.966
- The pressure's on.
- You think he's gonna lose?

262
00:16:11.633 --> 00:16:14.200
For some strange reason, that stinks.

263
00:16:14.266 --> 00:16:18.700
It feels like everything is going according to the way Sawyer planned it.

264
00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:19.966
It seems that way.

265
00:16:20.033 --> 00:16:22.533
Sawyer really has Ash all figured out.

266
00:16:22.766 --> 00:16:27.666
Yeah. Like Sawyer's taken everything he's learned from Ash to heart.

267
00:16:28.133 --> 00:16:30.100
All his hard work is paying off.

268
00:16:31.633 --> 00:16:34.066
Know what? Ash isn't going to lose.

269
00:16:34.866 --> 00:16:38.000
Nobody could ever duplicate the Ash we all know.

270
00:16:41.566 --> 00:16:42.633
Let's see.

271
00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.666
Okay, Pikachu, I choose you!

272
00:16:45.733 --> 00:16:46.633
Pikachu!

273
00:16:47.266 --> 00:16:49.633
And there's Ash's third Pokémon!

274
00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:52.800
So, now it's time for Pikachu.

275
00:16:53.266 --> 00:16:56.133
- Go for it, Pikachu!
- Dedenne!

276
00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.100
Chespin! Chespin!

277
00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:01.866
It's all up to you, buddy. Use the forest for cover!

278
00:17:01.933 --> 00:17:03.166
Pikachu!

279
00:17:03.233 --> 00:17:05.099
Pikachu makes the first move.

280
00:17:05.166 --> 00:17:07.233
Such incredible speed!

281
00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:10.066
Is this what it means to be lightning fast?

282
00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:12.400
All right. Thunderbolt, let's go!

283
00:17:13.166 --> 00:17:16.400
Pikachu!

284
00:17:16.466 --> 00:17:17.866
Dodge it, quick!

285
00:17:18.733 --> 00:17:21.033
- It dodged it.
- It's not over yet.

286
00:17:21.099 --> 00:17:22.400
Use Quick Attack!

287
00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:24.866
Dodge it, Clawitzer!

288
00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:30.100
Use Ice Beam!

289
00:17:30.566 --> 00:17:32.600
Clawitzer!

290
00:17:32.666 --> 00:17:34.366
- Dodge that!
- Chu!

291
00:17:34.866 --> 00:17:35.966
Use Electro Ball!

292
00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:38.600
- Pika, pika, pika.
- Clawitzer, Dragon Pulse!

293
00:17:39.166 --> 00:17:42.100
Clawitzer!

294
00:17:42.733 --> 00:17:43.566
Pika!

295
00:17:45.466 --> 00:17:48.133
Neither of them are backing down!

296
00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:50.566
We really need to beat Pikachu.

297
00:17:50.633 --> 00:17:52.766
That will give us a huge advantage.

298
00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:55.466
All right, Clawitzer, use Aqua Jet!

299
00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:58.733
- Into the forest!
- Pika! Pi, pi, pi...

300
00:18:03.066 --> 00:18:04.700
And now use Iron Tail!

301
00:18:05.366 --> 00:18:06.600
Pikachu!

302
00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:10.600
- Hurry and clamp it!
- Pika!?

303
00:18:12.200 --> 00:18:13.033
Pika?

304
00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:15.400
Clawitzer has Pikachu in its grasp!

305
00:18:15.466 --> 00:18:17.333
Stay there and use Water Pulse!

306
00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:20.400
Electro Ball!

307
00:18:20.866 --> 00:18:23.433
Pika, pika! Pi!

308
00:18:25.733 --> 00:18:27.266
Now use Thunderbolt!

309
00:18:27.933 --> 00:18:31.033
Pikachu!

310
00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:32.966
Clawitzer!

311
00:18:36.633 --> 00:18:37.500
Clawitzer!

312
00:18:39.466 --> 00:18:42.600
Clawitzer is unable to battle. Pikachu's the winner!

313
00:18:42.666 --> 00:18:44.200
- All right!
- Pika!

314
00:18:44.266 --> 00:18:47.200
Wow, Pikachu and Ash won! Hurray!

315
00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:49.200
Now it's two against two.

316
00:18:49.733 --> 00:18:50.700
Marvelous.

317
00:18:51.066 --> 00:18:53.466
Such an intriguing battle between them.

318
00:18:53.633 --> 00:18:54.700
One to remember.

319
00:18:54.866 --> 00:18:59.233
There is a strong bond of trust between both trainers and their Pokémon.

320
00:19:03.266 --> 00:19:04.866
You were great, Clawitzer.

321
00:19:06.333 --> 00:19:09.333
Now, this is what I expect from a battle with Ash.

322
00:19:10.033 --> 00:19:11.300
I'm glad you're back.

323
00:19:11.633 --> 00:19:13.366
You're the guy I look up to.

324
00:19:17.133 --> 00:19:20.566
Ash, you never fail to surprise me every single time.

325
00:19:21.033 --> 00:19:25.066
That was close, too close. It's 'cause of Pikachu that we won.

326
00:19:26.033 --> 00:19:27.066
Pika.

327
00:19:27.633 --> 00:19:30.300
So, what Pokémon are you gonna use next, huh?

328
00:19:30.766 --> 00:19:32.433
All right, Aegislash time!

329
00:19:33.733 --> 00:19:35.000
Aegislash.

330
00:19:35.966 --> 00:19:38.500
Sawyer's third Pokémon is Aegislash.

331
00:19:39.466 --> 00:19:43.500
Aegislash? I wonder how Ash is going to get past its King's Shield.

332
00:19:43.566 --> 00:19:45.300
Let's make it happen, buddy.

333
00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:48.366
- Get on back into the forest!
- Kachu!

334
00:19:52.266 --> 00:19:54.600
Aegislash, use Sacred Sword!

335
00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.033
Slash!

336
00:19:58.500 --> 00:19:59.333
Aegislash!

337
00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:01.333
Pika?

338
00:20:03.133 --> 00:20:03.966
Slash!

339
00:20:06.166 --> 00:20:09.333
Slash! Slash! Slash! Aegis!

340
00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:18.766
- What's going on?
- I'm not sure.

341
00:20:19.233 --> 00:20:21.333
Anything can happen at this point.

342
00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:23.666
Sawyer is serious about winning this.

343
00:20:23.966 --> 00:20:26.266
Be careful, Ash. Be careful.

344
00:20:27.033 --> 00:20:28.133
Pika.

345
00:20:31.233 --> 00:20:35.266
What will be the next move in Ash and Sawyer's long-awaited battle?

346
00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:37.166
How will it be resolved?

347
00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.166
And who will advance to the finals?

348
00:20:40.866 --> 00:20:45.533
More answers to come as the Kalos League journey continues.
